              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = 3x - 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " cuts the y-axis at C (0, –2)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.799,
            0.887,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We observe that any straight line written in the form y = ax + b cuts the y-axis at the point (0, b). The length b is referred to as the y-intercept of the line. Thus, the y-intercept of the line y = x + 3 is 3. This means that the line cuts the y-axis at a distance of 3 units from the origin in the positive direction. Similarly, the y-intercept of the line "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = 3x - 2\\  is  -2"
            }
          ]
        }
